From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James M Snell <jsnell@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:50:40 +0000
Subject: Implement DOMException and QuotaExceededError

Adds the WebIDL DOMException and QuotaExceededError interfaces as
globals of every context, and an API to create and read them without
running JavaScript: Exception::DOMException(),
Exception::QuotaExceededError(), Value::IsDOMException(),
Value::IsQuotaExceededError(), and the v8::DOMException and
v8::QuotaExceededError classes.

Instances are JS_ERROR_TYPE objects, so they capture a stack trace as
Error instances do and are native errors to Error.isError(). An API
caller that already has the stack, such as a deserializer, passes it
instead, and none is captured. Their attributes, the name's legacy
code included, are kept under private symbols at construction and
read by brand-checked prototype getters, which are CSA builtins.
NoSideEffectsErrorToString() reads the private slots, so the stack
header and the inspector show "name: message".

The globals are installed in InitializeGlobal(), not behind a flag in
InitializeExperimentalGlobal(), which is skipped in an isolate that
creates a snapshot: an embedder's snapshot would otherwise lack them.

